Q: How to add extra-host in windows container A: <p>I guess you've long solved this but including for anyone else having this issue, using Powershell <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.management/add-content?view=powershell-7.5" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Add-Content</a> worked for me:</p>
<pre><code>RUN powershell -Command &quot;Add-Content C:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\etc\\hosts '10.0.0.1 my.url-1.com'; Add-Content C:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\etc\\hosts '10.0.0.2 my.url-1.com'&quot;
</code></pre>

